course: dictionary
lesson: 1023
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. The word book is a good example. In «Sashko waves his exercise book in the air», book means a set of pages with writing, joined at one side inside a cover.
explain: Book can also mean a long written work. In «Borrowing books from the public library is free», the books are stories and texts you can read. Look at the words around the word to choose the right meaning.
explain: Book can be a verb, a doing word. In «Book a table for four», book means to arrange a place ahead of time. The word table and the idea of arranging help you see that this is not about reading. Ask yourself: is this a thing, or is someone doing something?
fact: Book (noun) means a set of pages with words or pictures, joined at one side inside a cover.
fact: Book (noun) can also mean a long written work, such as «a book about space».
fact: Book (verb) means to arrange a place or ticket ahead of time, as in «book a table».
fact: The verb forms are book, books, booked and booking.
fact: «By the book» means by the rules.
exercise: «Sashko waves his exercise book in the air.» What is an exercise book? | A machine that makes sounds | A kind of shoe | A place you reserve ahead of time | *A set of pages with writing, inside a cover
exercise: «Please book a table for four at seven o'clock.» What does book mean here? | A set of pages with words | To read quietly | *To arrange a place ahead of time | A long written story
exercise: «A shelf holds 10 books.» What does books mean in this sentence? | To reserve places ahead of time | Shelves in a library | *Things with pages and covers | To read aloud
test: «Borrowing books from the public library is free.» What does books mean here? | Reserved places | *Written works with pages | Pictures on a wall | Long walks
test: Nadia says, «I will book my seat on the train.» What does book mean? | To put a cover on | To count the pages | *To reserve ahead of time | To read a story
exam: «If a library book is damaged, you tell the librarian when you return it.» Which meaning of book fits best? | To arrange a place ahead of time | *A set of pages with words, joined inside a cover | A type of shoe | To shout loudly
